WEBVTT

00:01.417 --> 00:04.691
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.920 --> 00:08.194
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.228 --> 00:11.769
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.805 --> 00:14.777
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.812 --> 00:18.287
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.321 --> 00:21.595
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.629 --> 00:23.200
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.234 --> 00:24.837
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.871 --> 00:25.873
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.931 --> 00:36.335
Peter, come on,
get dressed.

00:36.369 --> 00:37.671
We're late
for church.

00:37.706 --> 00:39.308
I don't want to
go to church.

00:39.343 --> 00:41.882
I always feel like that
priest has it in for me.

00:41.916 --> 00:43.888
Body of Christ.

00:43.922 --> 00:45.893
Body of Christ.

00:45.927 --> 00:47.163
Butt of Christ.

00:47.197 --> 00:49.401
Aah! Lois, trade me.
No.

00:50.539 --> 00:52.710
You're not wearing that
to church, are you?

00:52.745 --> 00:54.080
What? Yeah. Why not?

00:54.115 --> 00:55.617
This is what
I always wear.

00:55.652 --> 00:56.854
She's right, man.

00:56.888 --> 00:58.024
It's Sunday. Get noticed.

00:58.058 --> 01:00.062
I'll be in the car.

01:01.434 --> 01:03.973
I'm getting tired of you wearing
the same thing every day.

01:04.007 --> 01:05.844
Look, that shirt's got
a hole in it.

01:05.879 --> 01:08.718
I'd like to point out that Jesus
wore the same thing every day.

01:08.752 --> 01:11.225
And you didn't hear Alice
giving him a hard time about it.

01:11.259 --> 01:12.528
Who?
Wasn't that her name?

01:12.562 --> 01:13.731
Let's just get to church.

01:13.765 --> 01:15.236
And afterward,
you're going to the mall

01:15.270 --> 01:16.404
to go clothes shopping.

01:16.439 --> 01:17.842
Well, you're
coming with me.

01:17.876 --> 01:20.282
Last time I tried shopping
without you, it was a disaster.

01:20.316 --> 01:21.652
Hey, I'm home.

01:21.686 --> 01:23.624
I got groceries.
You what?

01:23.691 --> 01:24.933
Yeah, I was driving past there,

01:24.961 --> 01:26.798
and we were out
of some stuff, so I...

01:26.833 --> 01:28.970
You listen to me,
you son of a bitch!

01:29.005 --> 01:30.943
I've got one thing
in this lifetime!

01:30.977 --> 01:32.747
One thing.

01:32.781 --> 01:35.755
You always say I never
do anything around here.

01:35.789 --> 01:39.097
Yeah, I like saying that more
than I like you doing things.

01:39.132 --> 01:41.336
Dad, I got the rest
from the car. Where...?

01:41.370 --> 01:42.739
Chris, run!
You were right!

01:42.774 --> 01:43.909
She didn't appreciate it!

01:43.943 --> 01:46.115
Oh, crap!

01:46.150 --> 01:47.852
Ow!

01:47.888 --> 01:49.190
That's right.

01:49.224 --> 01:50.860
I do groceries.

01:55.607 --> 01:57.545
All right, even though
we just walked in,

01:57.579 --> 02:00.486
and this whole place is one
hallway, let's consult the map.

02:00.520 --> 02:02.156
Okay.

02:02.191 --> 02:03.426
Uh-oh.

02:08.173 --> 02:11.314
I'll bet we can find you
some new clothes in here.

02:11.348 --> 02:13.987
Hey, Lois, are you sure
this place is for men?

02:14.021 --> 02:15.391
Yes, Peter, it's for everyone.

02:15.425 --> 02:17.697
Really? 'Cause this-this
kind of looks like a dress.

02:17.731 --> 02:19.869
Peter, it's fine.
Come on out.

02:20.873 --> 02:22.977
Ha! You gaybo!

02:25.552 --> 02:26.788
Hang on, Peter.

02:26.822 --> 02:29.260
I'm gonna go look for a couple
things for me in here.

02:29.294 --> 02:30.430
I'll be right back.

02:30.464 --> 02:31.834
Okay, Lois, I'll
be right here,

02:31.868 --> 02:34.474
standing uncomfortably close to
the unnecessary piano player

02:34.508 --> 02:36.245
in the middle of the mall.

02:38.017 --> 02:40.122
So, what's it like
now that you've made it?

02:40.156 --> 02:41.559
Did you ever have
a bank account

02:41.593 --> 02:43.297
full of pedestrians'
disinterested smiles?

02:43.331 --> 02:44.733
You're amazing.

02:44.768 --> 02:47.340
I'm gonna sit Indian-style
on top of your piano.

02:48.644 --> 02:51.418
There aren't enough verses
in any song I could write

02:51.452 --> 02:54.291
that would express how much
hatred I have in my heart.

02:54.326 --> 02:56.531
You talk like a book.

02:58.135 --> 02:59.472
Hey, Lois,
how about we try Sears?

02:59.507 --> 03:00.641
They got good stuff.

03:00.675 --> 03:02.179
Peter, nobody's been
in Sears for decades.

03:02.213 --> 03:03.917
Oh, come on.
When I was a boy,

03:03.951 --> 03:05.795
we always used to go
clothes shopping at Sears.

03:05.823 --> 03:07.492
Trust me. They'll have
everything I need.

03:13.041 --> 03:14.343
What the hell happened here?

03:14.378 --> 03:15.680
Look out!

03:19.992 --> 03:22.030
He wants to know
who you are.

03:22.065 --> 03:24.469
We seek clothes
for the cold times.

03:26.510 --> 03:29.449
He says he'll take you to
the clothes for herbs and meat.

03:29.483 --> 03:30.954
Well, we can probably come up

03:30.988 --> 03:32.892
with some herbs
and meat, right, Peter?

03:32.926 --> 03:34.329
Peter?

03:34.363 --> 03:35.799
I'm with them now.

03:35.833 --> 03:37.203
No girls allowed.

03:43.687 --> 03:45.625
See, Lois, now,
this is more like it.

03:45.659 --> 03:47.663
What the hell?
Why won't this button?

03:47.697 --> 03:49.368
It's the same size
I always get.

03:49.402 --> 03:51.306
Maybe you put on a
few pounds, sweetie.

03:51.340 --> 03:53.512
Lois, I weigh the same
293 pounds today

03:53.546 --> 03:54.815
that I weighed
in grade school.

03:54.850 --> 03:57.489
Perhaps it's this lump
on the side of your neck, sir.

03:57.523 --> 03:58.959
Oh, my God, Peter!

03:58.993 --> 04:00.764
How long have you
had that thing?

04:00.798 --> 04:01.933
I-I don't know.

04:01.968 --> 04:04.039
We got to go see
Dr. Hartman right away.

04:04.073 --> 04:05.910
Oh, my God, what if
it's something serious?

04:05.944 --> 04:07.314
It's all right,
it's all right.

04:07.349 --> 04:09.219
We'll be in good hands
with Dr. Hartman.

04:09.254 --> 04:11.191
He handled
my reassignment surgery.

04:11.259 --> 04:14.633
I think, emotionally, I've
always been a lizard, you know?

04:14.667 --> 04:16.137
And now, I feel
comfortable finally

04:16.172 --> 04:17.574
in my leathery,
scaly skin.

04:17.608 --> 04:19.078
Kids, if you need me,

04:19.112 --> 04:21.952
I'll be on the wall making
rapid, darting glances.

04:24.192 --> 04:26.597
Is this just to get out
of my parents' visit?

04:26.631 --> 04:27.767
No.

04:28.971 --> 04:30.975
Hello!

04:34.586 --> 04:36.423
<i>No, you're stupid!</i>

04:36.457 --> 04:37.860
Oh, hello, Griffins.

04:37.894 --> 04:39.531
What can I help
you with today?

04:39.565 --> 04:42.973
Dr. Hartman, Peter has a huge
lump growing on his neck.

04:43.007 --> 04:44.377
Mrs. Griffin,
that's called a "head."

04:44.411 --> 04:46.014
I've been fooled
by that one before.

04:46.048 --> 04:47.786
Well, will you
take a look at it?

04:47.820 --> 04:49.289
I think it might
be a tumor.

04:49.323 --> 04:50.727
Okay, let's
have a look.

04:51.763 --> 04:54.235
Oh, yes, it appears
that there is a...

04:54.270 --> 04:55.572
Great rack, by the way.

04:55.606 --> 04:56.809
Thank you.

04:56.843 --> 04:58.313
Well, thank Grandma
Griffin, really.

04:58.347 --> 05:01.086
It appears you have
a subcutaneous vestigial twin

05:01.121 --> 05:02.390
growing on your neck.

05:02.424 --> 05:03.760
What is that?

05:03.795 --> 05:05.164
Well, it's
an incomplete twin

05:05.199 --> 05:07.002
that never developed
into a fully-formed person

05:07.037 --> 05:09.341
but still exists as a growth
feeding off your body.

05:09.375 --> 05:10.611
Now, hold still.

05:10.645 --> 05:12.382
I'm just gonna give you
a little topical anesthetic,

05:12.417 --> 05:13.586
and we'll have
a closer look.

05:17.530 --> 05:18.565
Hi, everybody!

05:18.600 --> 05:20.303
Aah! What the
hell is that?!

05:20.338 --> 05:22.275
Oh, my God!
It's a little me!

05:22.309 --> 05:24.581
Well, it looks as if he's more
fully formed than we thought.

05:24.616 --> 05:27.088
Wow, your wife
is gorgeous!

05:27.122 --> 05:28.625
Is that a foot?

05:28.659 --> 05:29.794
Almost!

05:29.829 --> 05:31.064
This is awesome!

05:31.099 --> 05:32.736
Finally, I'll have an
interesting silhouette

05:32.770 --> 05:35.141
for the beginning of
my spoken-word jazz.

05:37.883 --> 05:39.854
I left...

05:39.888 --> 05:41.859
my poem...

05:41.893 --> 05:43.897
at home.

05:47.984 --> 05:50.823
<i>We now return to Quantum Creep.</i>

05:54.868 --> 05:56.839
Al, what year is it?

05:56.873 --> 05:58.844
1972.
Cool.

05:58.878 --> 06:01.317
I'm gonna go show my penis
to some kids.

06:01.351 --> 06:03.890
Hey, Dad. How'd it
go at the hospital?

06:03.925 --> 06:05.728
Kids, remember
how when you were little,

06:05.763 --> 06:07.300
you always wanted
a neck uncle?

06:07.334 --> 06:09.138
No.
Well, now you got one!

06:10.409 --> 06:11.844
What is that thing?!

06:11.879 --> 06:13.448
This is my vestigial twin.

06:13.483 --> 06:14.685
I named him Chip.

06:14.719 --> 06:16.423
You know, like
"chip off the old neck."

06:16.457 --> 06:18.529
I like to poke him
'cause it makes him happy,

06:18.563 --> 06:20.667
and I feel it a little bit
in my nads.

06:23.375 --> 06:24.979
Well, keep that freakish thing
under wraps.

06:25.013 --> 06:26.750
I don't want it
cramping my style

06:26.784 --> 06:28.253
while I'm macking on toddlers.

06:32.833 --> 06:34.803
See you around, bitch.

06:34.839 --> 06:37.210
You know, Lois, a lot of times
you go into someone's house,

06:37.244 --> 06:39.181
and it's just a house,
but you can tell

06:39.216 --> 06:41.688
this is a home
by all the love here.

06:41.722 --> 06:43.126
Aw! Aw!
Aw! Aw!

06:43.160 --> 06:45.799
Peter, this seems unnatural,
and, quite frankly, dangerous.

06:45.833 --> 06:48.339
Hey, you must be the owner
of that Prius outside.

06:48.373 --> 06:49.742
Thanks for saving
the world.

06:49.777 --> 06:51.146
He gets it.

06:51.181 --> 06:53.753
He gets what we Prius
owners are trying to do.

06:53.821 --> 06:55.858
Wow, the world
is such a cool place.

06:55.893 --> 06:57.863
There's so much
I want to do and see!

06:57.898 --> 07:00.437
Oh, he's such a great
energy to have around.

07:00.471 --> 07:03.511
Ah, Chip, I am gonna show you
all kinds of cool stuff.

07:03.546 --> 07:06.786
My Hot Wheels, my lawn darts,
even my new musket.

07:08.860 --> 07:10.931
Peter, what the
hell are you doing?

07:10.965 --> 07:13.036
Lois, I thought
I heard a noise downstairs.

07:13.070 --> 07:14.440
Go stall 'em for 20 minutes

07:14.475 --> 07:16.545
and pray that it's not
too damp in here.

07:18.551 --> 07:20.322
Man, how do you know
so many songs?

07:20.356 --> 07:22.327
Oh, when you're trapped
under a layer of fat,

07:22.361 --> 07:24.700
a muffled folk song
is like manna from Heaven.

07:24.734 --> 07:25.970
Give me a C.

07:27.642 --> 07:30.581
♪ Michael, row
the boat ashore ♪

07:30.616 --> 07:33.991
♪ Hallelujah

07:34.025 --> 07:37.166
♪ Michael, row the boat ashore

07:37.200 --> 07:40.072
♪ Hallelujah

07:40.107 --> 07:42.279
Sister, help
to trim the sail.

07:42.313 --> 07:45.453
♪ Sister, help
to trim the sail ♪

07:45.488 --> 07:48.461
♪ Hallelujah

07:48.496 --> 07:50.767
♪ Sister, help to trim...

07:52.038 --> 07:53.307
Aah! Run!

07:53.342 --> 07:56.749
No, Peter, gently stroke
his snout counterclockwise.

07:59.992 --> 08:01.662
Wow, it's working.

08:01.697 --> 08:04.202
There's a universal language
for all creatures,

08:04.237 --> 08:05.672
and it's called love.

08:05.707 --> 08:07.444
Now, how about
that River Jordan?

08:07.478 --> 08:10.920
♪ River Jordan
is deep and wide ♪

08:10.954 --> 08:13.893
♪ Hallelujah

08:13.928 --> 08:15.264
Join us, bear!

08:15.299 --> 08:18.372
♪ Milk and honey
on the other side ♪

08:18.406 --> 08:21.814
♪ Hallelujah.

08:26.260 --> 08:28.031
Good morning, boys.

08:28.065 --> 08:29.734
What's in store
for today?

08:29.770 --> 08:32.074
Well, I thought we'd start
with a vigorous power walk

08:32.108 --> 08:33.512
around the neighborhood.

08:33.546 --> 08:36.319
<i>Whoa, whoa, whoa. I was thinking
we would just watch Dr. Oz</i>

08:36.353 --> 08:38.190
and eat cold cuts
off our stomach.

08:40.931 --> 08:43.571
Those people ain't taking
good care of themselves.

08:43.605 --> 08:45.843
What?! But there's so much
to do and experience!

08:45.877 --> 08:47.113
Did you know

08:47.147 --> 08:49.151
that the Quahog Museum
has an interactive display

08:49.186 --> 08:50.856
on the history
of the garment district?

08:50.890 --> 08:52.573
Oh, look, Chip, Chip,
slow down, all right?

08:52.595 --> 08:54.232
You know, just because
everything's new to you

08:54.266 --> 08:56.204
doesn't mean
you have to do it all at once.

08:56.238 --> 08:58.242
Peter, where's your sense
of fun and adventure?

08:58.276 --> 09:00.447
You're starting to sound
like a stick-in-the-mud.

09:00.482 --> 09:02.152
Well, that stuff
sounds exhausting.

09:02.186 --> 09:04.525
I'm just being honest,
like George Washington.

09:04.559 --> 09:06.998
George, did you chop down
our cherry tree?

09:07.032 --> 09:09.304
I cannot tell
a lie. Yes.

09:09.339 --> 09:11.844
And what is this pamphlet
I found under your bed

09:11.879 --> 09:13.716
called "The Boston He Party?"

09:13.750 --> 09:15.486
Not mine.

09:20.100 --> 09:22.438
Wow! Is there any
better time in the world

09:22.472 --> 09:24.577
than 11:00 a.m.
on a Wednesday?

09:24.611 --> 09:27.451
You already have two days
of hard work under your belt,

09:27.485 --> 09:29.457
and there's so much
more work to come.

09:29.491 --> 09:31.628
Look, I'm trying to get
this stuff done here.

09:31.663 --> 09:33.835
Griffin, did you finish
those purchasing reports?

09:33.869 --> 09:35.505
Oh, that voice!

09:35.539 --> 09:37.143
It's like God sneezing!

09:37.177 --> 09:38.379
What the hell is this?

09:38.414 --> 09:40.016
They found a guy
on my neck.

09:40.051 --> 09:41.286
Hello there.

09:41.322 --> 09:43.861
I've never met a supervisor,
slash supermodel before.

09:43.895 --> 09:45.498
Do you like crab?

09:45.532 --> 09:48.071
There's a knockout crab place
right around the corner.

09:48.105 --> 09:49.441
What the hell are you doing?

09:49.475 --> 09:51.447
I'm using my knowledge
of the local food scene

09:51.481 --> 09:53.619
to get this woman
to go to bed with me.

09:54.656 --> 09:56.793
Well, now we know.

09:56.828 --> 09:59.133
I can taste
what he eats.

10:01.172 --> 10:03.478
What are we watching?
Oh, it's just a tennis match.

10:03.512 --> 10:05.316
So this is tennis!

10:05.350 --> 10:06.553
Wow!

10:06.587 --> 10:11.566
Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow!

10:11.600 --> 10:12.902
15-love.

10:12.937 --> 10:14.306
That was just one point?!

10:14.340 --> 10:17.079
Federer and Hastings are known
for their long rallies.

10:17.114 --> 10:18.383
Federer to serve.

10:18.418 --> 10:23.262
Wow! Wow! Wow!
Wow! Wow!

10:23.296 --> 10:25.335
Wow! Wow!

10:25.369 --> 10:29.278
Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow!

10:29.312 --> 10:30.681
<i>Wow!</i>

10:30.716 --> 10:31.851
15 all.

10:31.885 --> 10:33.288
And this is just
the first game

10:33.322 --> 10:35.427
of the first round
of a three-week tournament?

10:35.462 --> 10:36.731
Yay!

10:36.765 --> 10:38.401
This is more painful
than sitting

10:38.435 --> 10:40.707
through those
parent-teacher-cheetah meetings.

10:40.742 --> 10:42.980
So, in short, your kids
are all doing great.

10:43.015 --> 10:44.484
Keep reading to
them every night,

10:44.518 --> 10:46.723
and I think we're gonna
have a great year.

10:46.758 --> 10:48.160
So unless there
are any questions,

10:48.194 --> 10:49.430
thank you all
for coming.

10:49.464 --> 10:51.635
Uh, yeah, I noticed
the hot lunch menu

10:51.671 --> 10:53.473
doesn't feature
any gazelle.

10:54.711 --> 10:56.548
I'll bring that
up to the board.

10:56.582 --> 10:58.821
Yeah. See, I-I heard
that last year,

10:58.855 --> 11:01.796
and...
here we are again.

11:05.338 --> 11:06.809
Listen, Doc, is
there any way

11:06.843 --> 11:08.747
you can have this thing
on my neck removed?

11:08.781 --> 11:11.052
Well, Mr. Griffin, your organs
and his are intertwined.

11:11.087 --> 11:12.657
That would be a highly
dangerous procedure.

11:12.691 --> 11:13.960
You could die.

11:13.994 --> 11:15.732
On the other hand,
if you live,

11:15.766 --> 11:17.636
I'll let you pick any prize
off that shelf.

11:17.671 --> 11:19.207
Even the tiny
pinball machine?

11:19.241 --> 11:20.978
Oh, that-that shouldn't
have been up there.

11:21.012 --> 11:23.051
Look, Doc, you got to do
the procedure, all right?

11:23.085 --> 11:24.488
I-I don't care
if I die.

11:24.522 --> 11:26.091
I mean, maybe in
my next life,

11:26.126 --> 11:28.029
I'll come back as an
air bag or something.

11:32.977 --> 11:35.315
It's okay. It's okay.
Peter's got you.

11:35.350 --> 11:36.619
Don't you worry.

11:36.653 --> 11:38.223
Everything's gonna
be all right.

11:38.258 --> 11:39.584
Is my wife okay?

11:39.609 --> 11:41.612
No, the ski boots
that was in the back

11:41.633 --> 11:43.637
flew up and chopped
her head off.

11:43.671 --> 11:46.913
You can turn your blinker
off now; it's very annoying.

12:01.986 --> 12:03.856
Nurse, have somebody
fix that clock.

12:03.891 --> 12:05.025
It's very distracting.

12:05.060 --> 12:07.165
All right,
let's get this started.

12:14.017 --> 12:15.988
All right, halfway done.

12:16.022 --> 12:17.658
Time for a break.

12:22.605 --> 12:24.610
♪ I hate myself

12:24.645 --> 12:26.715
♪ For loving you

12:26.750 --> 12:28.487
♪ Can't break free

12:28.521 --> 12:30.859
♪ From the things
that you do... ♪

12:35.071 --> 12:37.176
Oh, God, I'm
so nervous.

12:37.210 --> 12:39.448
Thank God Stewie's too
little to understand.

12:39.482 --> 12:42.055
Look at him over there,
playing that board game.

12:42.089 --> 12:43.459
Ah, three.

12:43.493 --> 12:45.698
Okay, one, two...

12:45.732 --> 12:47.402
Sorry!

12:47.437 --> 12:50.744
<i>Sorry! The board game
that teaches you to be a dick.</i>

12:52.015 --> 12:54.420
Dr. Hartman, is everything
all right with my dad?

12:54.455 --> 12:56.927
Griffins, I'm
afraid we lost him.

12:56.961 --> 12:58.932
What?!
Oh, my God!

12:58.966 --> 13:00.703
Hey, guys.
Oh, there he is.

13:00.738 --> 13:02.742
It worked!
I'm free at last!

13:02.776 --> 13:04.814
But what about Chip?
Where's Chip?

13:04.849 --> 13:07.956
Hey, everybody,
look who's walking!

13:07.990 --> 13:09.793
Chip!

13:09.828 --> 13:12.299
Oh, Chip,
I'm so glad you're okay.

13:12.335 --> 13:14.138
Yeah, and I'm
okay, too.

13:14.172 --> 13:16.477
So, uh, you know, Chip,
now that you're a free man,

13:16.512 --> 13:18.349
this is a chance
for you to go out

13:18.383 --> 13:19.987
and make a real life
for yourself someplace.

13:20.021 --> 13:21.123
I'll tell you what,

13:21.158 --> 13:22.760
anywhere you want to
go, I'll FedEx you.

13:22.795 --> 13:24.432
What are you
talking about, Peter?

13:24.466 --> 13:26.437
Chip is part of our family.

13:26.471 --> 13:28.341
He's staying with us.
What?!

13:28.376 --> 13:30.548
Yay!
Yay! Awesome!

13:30.582 --> 13:32.419
Hey, hey, Dad?
Yeah, I'm done.

13:32.454 --> 13:34.291
Can you pick me up?

13:34.325 --> 13:36.329
Oh, that's okay;
I have a book.

13:43.269 --> 13:44.605
Oh, hey, Peter.

13:44.639 --> 13:46.108
Lois, where's the couch?

13:46.143 --> 13:48.615
Chip redecorated the room
to improve the feng shui.

13:48.649 --> 13:51.589
He said our old furniture was
blocking the flow of energy.

13:51.624 --> 13:54.229
I had my life's
fart savings in that couch!

13:54.264 --> 13:56.602
And where are the drapes?
Chip took them

13:56.637 --> 13:58.035
to make play clothes
for the children.

13:58.060 --> 13:59.176
What?!

14:04.290 --> 14:05.893
Oh, hey, Peter.
You're home.

14:05.928 --> 14:07.564
Hi, Dad!
Hi, Daddy.

14:07.599 --> 14:09.202
We dug a lake
for this!

14:09.236 --> 14:10.740
Whoa!

14:11.776 --> 14:13.546
Come out of that water at once!

14:13.581 --> 14:15.151
Gosh, isn't Chip
wonderful?

14:15.185 --> 14:16.855
No, he's not wonderful,
Lois; he's annoying.

14:16.889 --> 14:19.529
I don't get why everyone's
so in love with that guy.

14:19.563 --> 14:21.901
What's so great about him?
Well, to be honest,

14:21.935 --> 14:25.076
the same thing that used to be
so great about you.

14:25.110 --> 14:26.614
What? What are you
talking about?

14:26.648 --> 14:28.084
Just that when
you were younger,

14:28.118 --> 14:30.657
you were as passionate
and full of life as him.

14:32.663 --> 14:33.899
Hey, boys,

14:33.933 --> 14:36.105
catch me
if you can!

14:38.211 --> 14:40.283
Oh, crap!
I didn't realize they had bikes!

14:40.317 --> 14:42.555
What are they gonna do
when they catch me?

14:42.589 --> 14:44.761
Oh, boy, I got a
back-of-the-head punch coming,

14:44.795 --> 14:46.098
I just know it!

14:51.913 --> 14:54.887
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

14:54.921 --> 14:57.260
What the hell?
♪ Is violence in movies

14:57.294 --> 14:59.132
♪ And sex on TV

14:59.166 --> 15:02.673
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

15:02.708 --> 15:04.946
♪ On which we used to rely?

15:04.981 --> 15:07.152
What the...? What the
hell is going on here?

15:07.186 --> 15:08.956
You're singing our
song without me?

15:08.991 --> 15:10.895
Oh, sorry, Peter,
we couldn't find you.

15:10.929 --> 15:12.967
Do you want to sing
your part, Peter?

15:13.002 --> 15:14.504
Go ahead.

15:14.539 --> 15:16.710
♪ But where are
the fashioned ♪

15:16.745 --> 15:18.381
♪ Good fashion...

15:18.415 --> 15:21.055
I don't want to!

15:24.665 --> 15:26.402
I tell you,
Chip is making my life

15:26.436 --> 15:27.738
a living hell,
you guys.

15:27.773 --> 15:29.978
Remind me again, Chip is
that African kid you adopted?

15:30.012 --> 15:32.250
No, that was Chocolate Chip.
We gave him back to Kenya.

15:32.284 --> 15:34.924
But I can't take it anymore.
I got to get rid of him.

15:34.959 --> 15:36.929
Well, what are you gonna do?
I don't know yet,

15:36.964 --> 15:38.132
but I'll come up
with something.

15:38.167 --> 15:39.836
After all, I'm the guy
who invented

15:39.870 --> 15:42.076
"Choose Your Own Adventure
or Have Pie in Bed."

15:42.110 --> 15:44.181
I picked the pie again.

15:49.663 --> 15:53.238
<i>Hey, welcome back to
the Mikey Tony Magnanimous Hour,</i>

15:53.273 --> 15:55.845
where real people get
magnanimous about real things.

15:55.879 --> 15:58.285
This week's real thing--
hey, Native Americans,

15:58.319 --> 16:00.290
if I saw you
on the street begging,

16:00.324 --> 16:02.194
I'd throw a buck
in your moccasin.

16:02.229 --> 16:03.966
Next week's magnanimous thing--

16:04.000 --> 16:06.773
I'm wearing this yellow
bracelet. You're welcome.

16:06.807 --> 16:09.112
Peter, what the
hell is that thing?

16:09.147 --> 16:11.117
It's a dingo.
I named him Bingo.

16:11.152 --> 16:13.257
If you can't have fun
with that, you're crazy.

16:15.330 --> 16:16.432
Hey, Peter.

16:16.466 --> 16:17.768
Wh-What's that?

16:17.803 --> 16:20.408
Oh, he's gonna turn you
into a pile on Joe's lawn.

16:20.443 --> 16:22.447
What?!
Here, let's play steak catch.

16:22.481 --> 16:23.683
Oh, boy, I got it!

16:23.718 --> 16:25.020
Hey, back to you, Peter!

16:25.054 --> 16:26.758
Ah, cool! Steak catch!

16:26.792 --> 16:29.164
I'm gonna use my one
steak-in-the-pants time-out.

16:29.199 --> 16:31.537
Aah! No! Not me! Not me!

16:31.572 --> 16:33.041
Attack him! Aah!

16:33.075 --> 16:36.517
Hey, um, it's 3:00 p.m.
Should I give up on breakfast?

16:37.553 --> 16:38.655
Aah! Brian!

16:38.690 --> 16:40.092
Browser history--
clear it!

16:40.127 --> 16:43.902
Peter, that dingo was meant
to eat me, wasn't it?

16:43.937 --> 16:45.540
Why would you do that?

16:45.574 --> 16:48.013
Because my life was fine
before you showed up.

16:48.047 --> 16:50.453
My family liked me,
and-and I didn't feel bad

16:50.487 --> 16:52.191
about not ever doing new stuff.

16:52.225 --> 16:54.697
Well, I never asked to
grow out of your neck.

16:54.732 --> 16:57.738
My life was better
before I met you, too!

16:57.773 --> 17:00.646
You're a terrible brother,
husband and father.

17:00.680 --> 17:03.152
I'm out of here,
and you could go to hell!

17:03.187 --> 17:06.060
Wow, what a nice day out!
Look! A rainbow!

17:06.094 --> 17:07.597
I did it.

17:07.631 --> 17:09.034
He's gone.

17:09.069 --> 17:12.510
Just as easy as
the creation of techno music.

17:12.544 --> 17:14.482
Wait a minute,
what key are we in?

17:14.516 --> 17:16.520
No, no, no, no,
no, none of that.

17:21.300 --> 17:23.104
Oh, hey, Peter.
Where's Chip?

17:23.138 --> 17:24.876
I haven't seen him
all day.

17:24.910 --> 17:26.647
He likes to yell out
"Good luck!"

17:26.681 --> 17:28.451
after they read
each lottery number.

17:28.485 --> 17:30.089
He's gone.
I threw him out.

17:30.123 --> 17:31.325
You what?
No!

17:31.360 --> 17:33.163
Peter, how could you?

17:33.198 --> 17:35.235
Whoa, whoa, what are you all
coming down on me for?

17:35.270 --> 17:37.674
Meg throws away people who come
out of her body all the time,

17:37.676 --> 17:38.678
nobody says nothing.

17:38.712 --> 17:40.750
Peter, Chip was
a part of our family.

17:40.784 --> 17:41.920
And he's so little.

17:41.954 --> 17:44.058
He can get hurt
out there on his own.

17:44.092 --> 17:45.663
We got to go find him.

17:45.697 --> 17:48.002
We should look for him
in the ball pit at McDonald's.

17:48.037 --> 17:50.120
You can just leave me there;
I'll conduct the search.

17:50.142 --> 17:51.879
Meg's right!
Come on, kids,

17:51.913 --> 17:54.452
let's go find Chip
and bring him back!

17:54.486 --> 17:57.059
You guys do whatever you want.
I got stuff to do, anyway.

17:57.093 --> 17:59.064
I got to get ready
for my Bar Mitzvah.

17:59.098 --> 18:00.835
♪ Baruch atah Adonai

18:00.869 --> 18:03.508
♪ I want fancy things
like my friend Ephraim ♪

18:03.543 --> 18:05.146
♪ I want the newest
ten-speed bicycle ♪

18:05.181 --> 18:08.053
♪ That I will ride once, but
then I will call my parents ♪

18:08.089 --> 18:09.758
♪ And have them come get me

18:09.792 --> 18:12.899
♪ I want to swim in the pool
but only with my shirt on ♪

18:12.934 --> 18:14.971
♪ I want to lose
my virginity at 24 ♪

18:15.007 --> 18:16.609
♪ But tell everyone
I was 16... ♪

18:20.855 --> 18:23.560
Ah, crap, I'm out of beer.

18:24.865 --> 18:27.070
Great. I have to walk
down these stairs

18:27.104 --> 18:29.810
the one day I wore heels.

18:33.922 --> 18:35.224
Son of a bitch!

18:35.259 --> 18:37.063
I think I broke my leg!

18:39.570 --> 18:42.342
There's no way I'm gonna make it
back up those stairs.

18:45.017 --> 18:46.420
Nope.

18:48.025 --> 18:50.397
Peter? It's me, Chip.

18:50.431 --> 18:53.405
Listen, I... I'm sorry
for the mean things I said.

18:53.439 --> 18:55.610
Help!
Peter?

18:57.483 --> 18:59.721
Holy smokes!
Peter, are you okay?

18:59.756 --> 19:01.258
These books was already
down here!

19:01.292 --> 19:02.528
I'm not a nerd!

19:03.297 --> 19:04.634
Oh, my God!

19:04.668 --> 19:07.374
We got to get this leg set
and get you to the hospital!

19:07.408 --> 19:09.714
<i>Oh, cool. That's the place
with all the Ghostbusters cars!</i>

19:29.666 --> 19:31.904
If you had only done that
while you were here,

19:31.939 --> 19:33.408
we wouldn't be in this mess.

19:37.253 --> 19:39.224
Mr. Griffin,
you're a lucky man.

19:39.258 --> 19:42.097
If it weren't for Chip here,
you might have lost your leg.

19:42.131 --> 19:43.835
The bad news is,
we did an X-ray,

19:43.870 --> 19:46.208
and your body is full
of a spooky skeleton man.

19:46.243 --> 19:48.948
Gosh, Chip, I don't
know how to thank you.

19:48.983 --> 19:50.385
No problem, Peter.

19:50.419 --> 19:52.358
You would have done
the same thing for me.

19:52.392 --> 19:55.031
You know, Chip, Lois
was right about you.

19:55.065 --> 19:56.769
You are special.

19:56.803 --> 19:59.844
You've got all the sense of
wonder that I somehow lost.

19:59.878 --> 20:02.049
I got so used to watching TV

20:02.083 --> 20:04.289
and looking for tiny
jean fibers in my nuts,

20:04.323 --> 20:07.229
I forgot there's a whole
world out there to experience.

20:07.263 --> 20:08.833
Thank you for
showing me that.

20:08.868 --> 20:10.571
As far as I'm concerned,

20:10.606 --> 20:12.777
you're a permanent
part of our family now.

20:12.811 --> 20:15.517
Well, that sure is nice of you,
Peter, but...

20:15.552 --> 20:17.823
there's a big old world
out there.

20:17.857 --> 20:20.430
I want to go out
and experience it for myself.

20:20.464 --> 20:22.134
Aw!
Why?

20:22.169 --> 20:25.576
Well, I'm sorry to see you go,
but I understand.

20:25.611 --> 20:27.816
Oh, we're gonna miss you, Chip.

20:31.393 --> 20:35.202
I'm too tough to cry,
but I'm gonna miss you, too.

20:38.912 --> 20:41.183
Safe travels, buddy,
and keep in touch.

20:41.218 --> 20:42.554
I will!

20:42.589 --> 20:44.993
Whee!

20:45.028 --> 20:46.731
Good-bye, Chip!
Bye!

20:46.766 --> 20:48.904
Come back soon, okay?

20:48.938 --> 20:50.742
<i>But Chip never did come back.</i>

20:50.810 --> 20:54.980
<i>He became the new, young,
funny kid on ABC's The Middle.</i>

20:57.298 --> 20:59.302
Wow! This is just a whole
bunch of loud garbage!

20:59.303 --> 22:00.303
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru